From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] va: retain the deployed AV1 capability boundary

The upstream SM8550 qualification does not establish support on every Iris
firmware. Keep AV1 unadvertised until the target decoder has been qualified.

Co-Authored-By: gpt-6-astra <noreply@openai.com>

--- a/src/va/driver.cc
+++ b/src/va/driver.cc
@@ -147,6 +147,10 @@
     if (caps.output_formats.count(V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1) && caps.nv12)
         caps.import_formats.insert(V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1);
     // import-qualified-end
+    // Preserve the deployed decode capability boundary during the encoder
+    // upgrade. AV1 needs its own target-device qualification.
+    caps.profiles.erase(VAProfileAV1Profile0);
+    caps.import_formats.erase(V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1);
     // VP9 is absent from default qualification: the session-side blocker is
     // gone — lending one picture one buffer per completion ran clean on the
     // target (FFmpeg 515/515, misplaced=0, framemd5 equal to the software
